ity for reviews. The engineer plan should pick one. A maintainer may want to confirm it, because it changes the merge gate.\n- The bot-commit audit workflow under .github/ should only be documented, not changed. Agents may not modify .github/, and it is a protected path.\n- There are no architect, product-manager or documentation-planner roles, but this change is user-visible and crosses several packages. The engineer plan has to cover those concerns too.\n\nRequested next: `ard:triage:engineer`\nOutput: [.ard/302/triage-lead.md](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/ca8578f4d6024fff91c952cea15524e0cbcd6e01/.ard/302/triage-lead.md) · log [.ard/302/logs/triage-lead-20261124T175738.098Z.log](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/ca8578f4d6024fff91c952cea15524e0cbcd6e01/.ard/302/logs/triage-lead-20261124T175738.098Z.log) · job `01M87B9GKNQKEDTVJJ4K1BX0AS` · attempt 1\n\n\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01H2N6R44RSPVu3hdJyW8zdR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
