{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNK9h2FgncDKriUrtS4s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the plan for #302 to `.ard/302/plan.md` and the status file to `.ard/302/triage-engineer.md`. The status is done, the size is L and the risk is medium. I didn't run any code or tests; the plan comes from reading the repository.\n\n- **Plan:** it adds a connectivity check in `internal/github/connect.go` and a `gh` fallback in `internal/github/ghcli.go`. It also changes `buildDeps` in `internal/servecmd/serve.go`, adds an identity line to `ard config check`, and updates the docs.\n- **Self-review decision:** I chose to make no reviewer or merger logic change. The reviewer already posts every review as a comment. The merger's `approved()` in `internal/merger/gates.go` already ignores approvals from ard's own login, which under a token is the token's user. So a token setup needs protected-path approvals from a different user with write access. The docs state this and a test pins it.\n- **Open issues posted to the issue:**\n  - A maintainer should confirm the self-review decision.\n  - `CLAUDE.md` still describes GitHub access as an App installation token. It is a protected path, so someone has to update it by hand.\n  - The bot-commit workflow under `.github/` is only documented, not changed.\n\nOne format wrinkle: the self-review decision sits as a short paragraph under `## Implementation`, before `### Steps`, rather than inside one of the four subsections."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5281,"cache_read_input_tokens":35374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5281},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessio